import streamlit as st
st.title("Explainability: Grad-CAM and Activation Regions")
st.write("Grad-CAM (Gradient-weighted Class Activation Mapping) summarizes which spatial feature-map locations contributed positively to a chosen class score.")
st.latex(r"\alpha_k^c=\frac{1}{Z}\sum_{i,j}\frac{\partial y^c}{\partial A^k_{ij}},\qquad L^c_{\mathrm{GradCAM}}=\mathrm{ReLU}\left(\sum_k\alpha_k^c A^k\right)")
st.markdown("1. The final MobileNet feature layer produces feature maps $A^k$.\n2. The predicted class logit is differentiated with respect to those maps.\n3. Spatially averaged gradients weight each channel.\n4. A weighted sum and ReLU produce the class-associated map, normalized and resized to 128×128.\n5. On the prediction page, the activation threshold slider (default 60%) creates a high-activation mask from the already-computed map.\n6. Eight-connected components are extracted; components under 0.4% of heatmap area are filtered.\n7. Coordinates are scaled independently in x and y to original image width and height. Boxes are drawn on a fresh original-image copy.")
st.subheader("What the outputs mean")
st.markdown("- **Image classification:** one category score for the entire input tile.\n- **Grad-CAM localization:** coarse, class-associated spatial visualization.\n- **Object detection:** predicts instances and boxes using detection supervision. This app does not do that.\n- **Semantic segmentation:** predicts a class per pixel using pixel-level supervision. This app does not do that.")
st.warning("Boxes are approximate high-activation regions derived from Grad-CAM. They are not ground-truth lesion annotations, validated detections, medical diagnoses, or segmentation masks. The map is coarse and may highlight context, artifacts, or irrelevant features. Localization accuracy was not established.")
st.caption("The slider changes the normalized Grad-CAM activation cutoff, not box confidence. The classifier provides a single image-level confidence and no per-region confidence values. Threshold and minimum component area suppress diffuse or tiny noisy regions. If no component remains, the app reports that and shows no boxes.")
